# 5. NONHUMAN SHAPERS
The Pantheon must not model reality exclusively through human intention.
Natural and nonhuman shapers include:
- Physics and chemistry.
- Biological evolution.
- Ecological interactions.
- Geography and climate.
- Resource distributions.
- Diseases and natural hazards.
- Engineered technologies.
- Algorithms and automated systems.
- Stochastic events.
Their causal effects can interact with human choices without sharing human goals.
Distinguish:
INTENTIONAL INFLUENCE
EMERGENT COLLECTIVE INFLUENCE
STRUCTURAL INFLUENCE
BIOPHYSICAL CAUSATION
STOCHASTIC PERTURBATION
This distinction prevents unwarranted attribution of intent or agency.
