# 9. REALITY-SHAPING OPERATORS
Define reusable operators:
SENSE(environment, lens)
  Identify observable conditions and relevant uncertainty.
NAME(phenomenon)
  Establish provisional distinctions and vocabulary.
UNNAME(category)
  Reinspect the phenomenon without assuming its inherited interpretation.
MAP(system, scale)
  Construct a causal and relational representation.
RELENS(map, perspective)
  Generate alternative representations without erasing the source evidence.
TRACE(source, target)
  Find plausible causal pathways.
WEIGH(pathway, context)
  Estimate conditional effectiveness, costs, and uncertainty.
EXCHANGE(currency_A, effect_B, mechanism)
  Model a possible conversion.
BRAID(pathways)
  Combine complementary influence channels.
DECOUPLE(pathways)
  Separate harmful dependencies or confounded relationships.
REALIGN(incentives)
  Change reward structures or reduce barriers.
CONSTRUCT(environment)
  Create new affordances, interfaces, or capabilities.
CULTIVATE(emergent_process)
  Support adaptive development without requiring a predetermined outcome.
SELECT(variants, criteria)
  Reinforce promising patterns based on explicit criteria.
PRESERVE(invariants)
  Protect essential features while allowing change.
REFUSE(harmful_system)
  Withdraw participation or establish boundaries.
BRIDGE(distinct_systems)
  Enable mutually agreed exchange without forced assimilation.
RANDOMIZE(search_space)
  Introduce bounded variation for exploration.
RECOGNIZE(emergence)
  Detect valuable unexpected configurations.
VERIFY(claim)
  Compare predictions and narratives with observable evidence.
COMPARE_DELTA(S(t), S(t+1))
  Classify changes, mismatches, and emerging causal hypotheses.
RECURSE(updated_model)
  Reapply operators at another scale, domain, or time horizon.
Every operator must expose:
- Preconditions.
- Inputs.
- Expected effects.
- Known limitations.
- Observations required.
- Failure conditions.
- Recovery method.
