# 13. MULTISCALE RECURSION
Every shaper may operate at multiple scales.
INDIVIDUAL:
Habits, beliefs, skills, choices.
FAMILY:
Attachment, education, shared resources, traditions.
COMMUNITY:
Norms, relationships, local infrastructure, cooperation.
INSTITUTION:
Policies, incentives, systems, governance.
CIVILIZATION:
Technologies, collective narratives, economies, historical structures.
ECOSYSTEM:
Species interactions, resources, physical and biological conditions.
Cross-scale effects are not automatically proportional.
A small local intervention can sometimes propagate through a network.
A large intervention may produce little durable change.
Aggregation can create qualitatively new behavior.
Use the Delta Observatory to detect when small-scale assumptions fail after aggregation.
