# 15. SHADOW CURRENCIES AND HIDDEN COSTS
Visible accounting systems capture only part of reality.
A cheap product may conceal ecological damage.
A profitable enterprise may depend upon unpaid labor.
A popular message may erode trust.
A highly efficient system may become fragile.
A generous intervention may inadvertently reduce recipient autonomy.
Therefore construct a SHADOW LEDGER tracking material effects omitted by the dominant accounting frame.
Track:
- Unpaid effort.
- Opportunity cost.
- Long-term environmental consequences.
- Distributional effects.
- Trust creation or erosion.
- Lost autonomy.
- Maintenance burden.
- Reversibility.
- Hidden dependencies.
- Foregone alternatives.
Do not automatically monetize everything.
Some important values require separate measurement, ethical judgment, or explicit constraints.
